    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0362" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.6711/7–745</note>
                <head>No. 196 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Embassy to the Department of State
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d196-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d196-f2"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p> Sir A. Clark Kerr has accordingly been instructed to point out to the Soviet
                    Government that, as they are aware, the Turkish Government have consulted His
                    Majesty’s Government about the recent Turco-Soviet conversations. … They wish
                    the Soviet Government to be aware of their views on these recent developments as
                    they consider the whole question will have to be discussed at <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Terminal</hi>.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-07">7th July,
                            1945</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d196-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d196-f1-content">
                <p>The gist of this memorandum was included in telegram No. 11 of July 10 from Grew
                    to Byrnes (file No. 740.00119 Potsdam/7–1045).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d196-f2" n="2" xml:id="d196-f2-content">
                <p>For the full text of this memorandum, see <ref target="#d704">document No.
                        704</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
